hey guys i'm abby Sharpe welcome to  Abby's kitchen so as a lot of you know I  am a bit of a fitness buff I love to  lift heavy things and spin and go to bar  class and legree I'm all over it  so when I started to see all those  commercials for like the Fitbit and all  my friends had it I was like oh my gosh  I need to get one of these I was totally  into it  but I want to tell you a little bit of a  story on how my Fitbit actually kind of  made me less fit so if you're not really  familiar with these fitness trackers I  want to tell you how they work basically  they track things like the steps you've  taken your distance your active minutes  your food your water your sleep and I  was really not interested in tracking  like my food and my sleep that would  have been pretty depressing but I was  pretty anal about tracking those steps  and when I first started out I was  pretty happy with like 13,000 steps a  day but then I started get super  competitive because that's just my  nature and then it was like 15,000 then  I wanted to get 18,000 some days I was  even getting 20,000 and that soon became  my normal I was always pushing to get  more and more and more so you'd think  that I was gonna get more fit by using  this fitness tracker but actually that's  not what my measurements were telling me  in fact my conditioning was declining my  strength was declining my muscle mass  was declining and I was actually gaining  body fat so there's a few reasons for  this and some mistakes that I made that  I want to tell you about so that  hopefully you can avoid them yourself so  first of all in order for me to meet  these super high stepping goals I had to  basically spend a lot more time during  this low-intensity walking when I could  have been spending that time on mobility  or spinning or weight training or  high-intensity interval training and I  know I've talked about this before but  research suggests that when you're doing  a ton of this low intensity cardio  without the proper nutrition to kind of  support it or of course strength  training to help balance it out you can  very easily cut into your games and what  I mean by this is when you're not doing  a lot of strength training to balance  out that low intensity cardio or you're  not nutritionally supporting that amount  of  you can actually start to burn through  your muscle so even if it seems like  you're burning a ton of calories as you  step and step and step and step on your  Fitbit if you're burning through your  muscle you're actually gonna be killing  your calorie and fat burning potential  in the long term which just takes you  farther and farther away from your  health goals so second of all I wasn't  really listening to my body's need for  pleasurable activity things that I  actually enjoyed doing I mean the  stepping routine got pretty boring  pretty fast and I just kept at it I mean  once I had met those those that gold all  those steps I was after I felt like I  was I was good for the day and I didn't  have any more room in my life for things  that I enjoyed like yoga or pilates or  spinning or picking up heavy weights so  yeah my Fitbit and I didn't really work  out but I do have some tips for helping  to make it work for you so first of all  do not pay attention to calories they  usually are overestimated on a lot of  these fitness trackers especially if you  sync it up to like your food journal  like a MyFitnessPal you often will  overestimate how many calories you need  to eat so just listen to your body  instead for those signs that you want  more activity or maybe you've had enough  so number two input your strength  training activities I know that they  don't burn as many calories or  contribute to steps but if you're a goal  oriented person like me it's really nice  to set some goals for you know how heavy  your lifting or how many reps you're  doing and actually to see some progress  in your fitness being made and you can  do that with your Fitbit number three  use it as a guide to build habits one of  the things I did like about my Fitbit  was it really opened my eyes to how  sedentary I often am when I'm not going  to the gym so it definitely did help to  instill some new healthy habits like you  know take the stairs or perks farther  away at the grocery store so once you've  built some these habits into your usual  routine you probably won't need a device  to fall back on number four I think  quality over quantity  so maybe set your goal a little bit  lower for steps than you think you can  accomplish knowing that some of your  activities may not contribute steps but  actually may be better Fitness builders  and muscle builders or fat burners so  for example you could try doing a  shorter set of you  both on the treadmill instead of a  really long leisurely walk which may  give you fewer steps but could give you  better fitness and metabolism benefits  and fat burning and number five don't  get obsessed if you're finding that  having an external indicator your  fitness is getting in the way of you  listening to your body then it's  probably not the best method for you I  know a lot of us like me we really need  some kind of accountability something to  look forward to some kind of goal to set  but there's a lot of other ways you  could do this maybe you know you've got  a friend you want to hook up with that  you can work out together you can set  goals together and you can of course  support each other if you aren't quite  getting to those goals so that's just an  idea but everybody's different when it  comes to fitness so definitely find what  works best for you  so guys I hope my story was helpful  whenever I share this story I always get  a ton of feedback from people telling me  that they've got similar experiences  with their fitness tracker and actually  getting rid of it has been beneficial  for them but I'm curious to hear from  you guys so leave me a comment below I  want to know what your experience with  your fitness trackers been like what  else have you been using what's been  working what's not been working also be  sure to give this video the thumbs up if  you liked it subscribe to the channel  and I'll see you next time on Abby's  kitchen  [Music]
 

